      "lazy": null,
      "note": "The documentation *corpus* is private — it is served by the API behind the owner allow-list — but this route is still declared above the wildcard below, and deliberately. `AuthGate` claims every path it reaches and bounces a signed-out visitor to the public home page with no explanation. A reader who bookmarked a documentation page and later signed out would simply find themselves somewhere else. Rendering the shell instead lets the surface say what actually happened — the corpus is private, sign in as the owner — which is the more useful answer and gives nothing away: every byte of the corpus arrives from an authenticated request, so an anonymous visitor reaches an empty frame and a sentence. It also mounts outside `Shell` and `ToastProvider`, alongside the entity catalog, because a reading surface has no workspace chrome to inherit.",
